# web lint conventions

This app is **Vite + React**, not Next.js. CI runs `cd web && pnpm run lint`.

## Do

- Run `pnpm run lint` in `web/` before pushing UI changes
- Use plain `<img>` when needed — never `@next/next/*` eslint directives
- Put co-located non-component exports (variants, hooks) in `components/ui/` (rule relaxed) or add a file-level `react-refresh/only-export-components` disable with a one-line reason
- Prefer deriving UI state over `setState` at the top of `useEffect` (`react-hooks/set-state-in-effect`). Defer loading flags with `await Promise.resolve()` / async IIFE, or clear selection in event handlers
- Empty `catch` blocks need a comment: `catch { /* why ignored */ }`

## Don't

- Port Next.js-only eslint disables or `next/image` assumptions into this Vite app
- Silence CI lint with broad `eslint-disable` at the top of unrelated files
- Add new UI packages or Next layers under `web/` unless asked
